# THREE build families use the REPO ROOT as their Docker context:
#   - install-smoke clean rooms (install-smoke/*.Dockerfile) — need install-smoke/
#   - the dashboard image (frontend/Dockerfile) — needs the npm workspace
#     manifests + packages/ + frontend/ sources
#   - the backend API image (backend/Dockerfile, as of B.1/B.2 21c39486) —
#     needs backend/ + the sibling packages/yoru-contract/ path-dep
#     (DEC-yoru-design-ruling-1 §C); it moved off the old `./backend`-only
#     context specifically so that sibling package is reachable.
# Everything else (the 5GB+ of backend/data/*.db, node_modules, .worktrees,
# build output, .git) would just bloat the context — and a live SQLite file
# mid-write even breaks the tar. Keep the context tiny + deterministic.
# marketing/ stays excluded: frontend/Dockerfile prunes missing workspaces, so
# the dev tree builds the same way the filtered public mirror does.
# A `.dockerignore` only applies at the CONTEXT root — per-directory copies
# are INERT once the context is root, which is why `backend/.dockerignore`
# was retired: its rules had to move HERE (below) or they'd silently stop
# applying — a `backend/.env` or `backend/data/*.db` landing in the root
# build context unnoticed is a real secret-adjacent leak risk, not just bloat.
*
!install-smoke
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!packages
!frontend
!backend
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.env*

# --- backend/ (was backend/.dockerignore, now dead — merged here) ---
backend/data/
backend/logs/
backend/*.db
backend/*.db-journal
backend/*.db-wal
backend/*.db-shm
backend/*.bak
backend/*.orig
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/**/*.pyc
backend/**/*.pyo
backend/**/*.pyd
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/.mypy_cache/
backend/**/*.egg-info/
backend/build/
backend/dist/
backend/**/tests/
backend/.venv/
backend/venv/
backend/env/
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example
backend/**/*.md
!backend/README.md
backend/.idea/
backend/.vscode/
backend/.DS_Store
